    "title": "Thanongchai Siriapisith - ACL Anthology",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "![ACL Logo](https://aclanthology.org/images/acl-logo.svg) ACL Anthology ⟨1⟩\n  * About⟨2⟩\n    * Announcements⟨3⟩\n    * Communication channels⟨4⟩\n    * Related work⟨5⟩\n    * Copyright⟨6⟩\n    * * * *\n    * Credits⟨7⟩\n    * Volunteer⟨8⟩\n    * Development⟨9⟩\n    * Feedback⟨10⟩\n  * Using⟨2⟩\n    * Citing papers⟨11⟩\n    * Links in the Anthology⟨12⟩\n    * Data access⟨13⟩\n    * * * *\n    * All FAQs⟨14⟩\n    * * * *\n    * ###### Details\n    * Anthology identifiers⟨15⟩\n    * Names⟨16⟩\n    * ORCID iDs⟨17⟩\n    * DOIs⟨18⟩\n    * Verified authors⟨19⟩\n  * Contributions⟨2⟩\n    * Submissions⟨20⟩\n    * Corrections⟨21⟩\n    * Author pages⟨22⟩\n    * Attachments⟨23⟩\n  * GitHub⟨24⟩\n\n\n##  Thanongchai Siriapisith ⟨22⟩\n* * *\n#### 2024\npdf ⟨25⟩bib ⟨26⟩abs⟨27⟩\n**SICAR at RRG2024: GPU Poor’s Guide to Radiology Report Generation⟨28⟩**  \nKiartnarin Udomlapsakul⟨29⟩ | Parinthapat Pengpun⟨30⟩ | Tossaporn Saengja⟨31⟩ | Kanyakorn Veerakanjana⟨32⟩ | Krittamate Tiankanon⟨33⟩ | Pitikorn Khlaisamniang⟨34⟩ | Pasit Supholkhan⟨35⟩ | Amrest Chinkamol⟨36⟩ | Pubordee Aussavavirojekul⟨37⟩ | Hirunkul Phimsiri⟨38⟩ | Tara Sripo⟨39⟩ | Chiraphat Boonnag⟨40⟩ | Trongtum Tongdee⟨41⟩ | Thanongchai Siriapisith⟨42⟩ | Pairash Saiviroonporn⟨43⟩ | Jiramet Kinchagawat⟨44⟩ | Piyalitt Ittichaiwong⟨45⟩  \nProceedings of the 23rd Workshop on Biomedical Natural Language Processing⟨46⟩\nRadiology report generation (RRG) aims to create free-text radiology reports from clinical imaging. Our solution employs a lightweight multimodal language model (MLLM) enhanced with a two-stage post-processing strategy, utilizing a Large Language Model (LLM) to boost diagnostic accuracy and ensure patient safety. We introduce the “First, Do No Harm” SafetyNet, which incorporates Xraydar, an advanced X-ray classification model, to cross-verify the model outputs and specifically address false negatives from the MLLM. This comprehensive approach combines the efficiency of lightweight models with the robustness of thorough post-processing techniques, offering a reliable solution for radiology report generation. Our system achieved fourth place on the F1-Radgraph metric for findings generation in the Radiology Report Generation Shared Task (RRG24).\nSearch⟨47⟩\n##### Co-authors\n  * Pubordee Aussavavirojekul⟨37⟩ 1\n  * Chiraphat Boonnag⟨40⟩ 1\n  * Amrest Chinkamol⟨36⟩ 1\n  * Piyalitt Ittichaiwong⟨45⟩ 1\n  * Pitikorn Khlaisamniang⟨34⟩ 1\nshow all...\n  * Jiramet Kinchagawat⟨44⟩ 1\n  * Parinthapat Pengpun⟨30⟩ 1\n  * Hirunkul Phimsiri⟨38⟩ 1\n  * Tossaporn Saengja⟨31⟩ 1\n  * Pairash Saiviroonporn⟨43⟩ 1\n  * Tara Sripo⟨39⟩ 1\n  * Pasit Supholkhan⟨35⟩ 1\n  * Krittamate Tiankanon⟨33⟩ 1\n  * Trongtum Tongdee⟨41⟩ 1\n  * Kiartnarin Udomlapsakul⟨29⟩ 1\n  * Kanyakorn Veerakanjana⟨32⟩ 1\n\n\n##### Venues\n  * BioNLP⟨48⟩1\n  * WS⟨49⟩1\n\n\n Fix author⟨50⟩\n![Creative Commons License](https://i.creativecommons.org/l/by/4.0/88x31.png)⟨51⟩ ACL materials are Copyright © 1963–2026 ACL; other materials are copyrighted by their respective copyright holders. Materials prior to 2016 here are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 International License⟨52⟩. Permission is granted to make copies for the purposes of teaching and research. Materials published in or after 2016 are licensed on a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License⟨53⟩.\nThe ACL Anthology is managed and built by the ACL Anthology team⟨7⟩ of volunteers.\n_Site last built on 22 July 2026 at 14:46 UTC withcommit 280e4ed⟨54⟩._\n",
